.\" Man page for magicdl. PUBLIC DOMAIN (CC0-1.0)
.TH MAGICDL 1 "@DATE@" "magicdl @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
magicdl \- index, download, and organize purchased digital collections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magicdl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B magicdl
keeps a local index of the content you own on supported stores, downloads what
is new, and verifies what is already on disk. It tracks multiple versions of an
item, records removed, hidden, and pre-ordered content, and stores a SHA\-256
per downloaded file so moved files can be relocated and integrity checked.
.PP
A run selects a backend with
.B \-\-backend
and supplies that backend's credentials. The state lives in a SQLite index
named by
.BR \-\-db .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list\-backends
List the available backends.
.TP
.B bundles
List the bundles a backend offers for
.BR \-\-bundle ,
one per line as "reference  description". For itch.io these are the account's
owned bundles, each with a bundle link to pass to
.BR \-\-bundle .
.TP
.B creators
List the creators in the local index for a backend, one per line with how many
items are owned from each, to pass a name to
.BR \-\-creator .
Reads the index only, so run
.B index
first.
.TP
.B index
Fetch the list of owned content and store it, without downloading files. With
.B \-\-hashes
it also resolves each item's files from the store and records their hashes in
the index, so
.B reorganize \-\-hash
can match loose files offline. That pass is paced and resumable: it skips items
whose hashes are already stored and commits after each one.
.TP
.BI "sync " "[id...]"
Download content. With no arguments it lists the whole collection from the
store and downloads what is new. With item ids it resolves only those from the
index. With
.B \-\-from\-index
it downloads what is already indexed without contacting the store's listing,
narrowed by the list filters (for example
.BR \-\-not\-downloaded ).
Items already downloaded in full are skipped without contacting the store, so a
repeat run resumes quickly;
.B \-\-refresh
re\-resolves them to pick up a store\-side re\-upload.
.TP
.B verify
Check downloaded files. Mark each present or missing;
.B \-\-rehash
re\-hashes present files to detect changed content;
.B \-\-rescan
hashes the output tree and relocates files that were moved, matched by hash.
.TP
.BI "check " "[id...]"
Compare local copies to the store's current version by hash, reporting each item
as current, outdated (a local file differs), incomplete (missing a current
file), or not\-downloaded. Unlike
.BR verify ,
which checks against what magicdl recorded, this asks the store, so it catches
updates to downloaded or adopted items. It resolves and hashes each item; scope
it with item ids or the list filters. Bandcamp offers no per\-file hash and
unpacks its albums, so for Bandcamp this confirms an item's files are present
rather than hashing them.
.TP
.B status
Show a summary of the collection: item and version counts, per\-format and
per\-backend breakdowns, and total size.
.TP
.B list
List items, one per line, with filters such as
.BR \-\-status ", " \-\-not\-downloaded ", and " \-\-limit .
.TP
.BI "details " id
Show one item's versions and the files under each.
.TP
.BI "blacklist " "id..."
Mark items so
.B sync
skips them. Add
.B \-\-reason
to note why.
.TP
.BI "allow " "id..."
Remove items from the blacklist.
.TP
.BI "relocate " "old new"
Record that an item moved from one id to another. The old item is skipped by
.BR sync .
.TP
.BI "forget " "id..."
Clear the adopted mark on the given items, so
.B sync
no longer skips them and will fetch them again. The files on disk are left in
place; this only forgets that magicdl treated the item as already owned
locally. Use it to refresh an item adopted from an archive once the store has a
newer version. An item that was not adopted is reported and left unchanged.
.TP
.BI "reorganize " dir
Fold loose files in a path\-based archive into the per\-item subfolders the
backend expects, so
.B import
can then adopt them. For each
.IR <user> .itch.io/
host that owns exactly one indexed item, the files sitting directly under the
host are moved into
.IR <user> .itch.io/ <slug> .
This pass is offline.
.IP
With
.B \-\-hash
it also handles a host that owns several items, where a loose file cannot be
placed by path alone. It matches each loose file's hash against the store-side
upload hashes and moves it under the slug whose upload it matches. A loose file
matching no upload is left in place. The upload hashes come from the index:
populate them once with
.B index \-\-hashes
and this pass runs entirely offline. Without them it resolves a host's items from
the store on the spot and caches the hashes, so the next run is offline.
.BI \-\-max\-owned " n"
skips a host that owns more than
.I n
items, to avoid resolving a large shared host. Slug subfolders and other
directories are left alone.
.IP
.B \-\-hash\-cross\-host
goes further: it matches each remaining loose file against the stored hashes of
every owned item, on any host, and moves it under that item's real slug folder.
This recovers files sitting in a folder whose name no longer matches the item's
host, for example when a creator renamed their itch username, which the per-host
pass cannot see. It is offline and uses only stored hashes, so run
.B index \-\-hashes
first. Only itch.io, which imports by path, supports this. Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to review the moves first.
.TP
.BI "import " dir
Adopt a hand\-built archive: mark indexed items whose files already sit under
.IR dir ,
so
.B sync
skips them. Index the collection first. itch.io matches its own
.IR <user> .itch.io/ <slug>
download layout by a direct path lookup; other backends match an
.IR Artist / "YYYY \- Album"
music library by name. Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to review matches before marking.
.TP
.B manifest
Write a browsable library manifest, one section per backend, in Markdown
(default) or HTML with
.BR \-\-html .
Each item is a checkbox, ticked when the index records it as downloaded, so run
.B verify
first for an accurate picture.
.B \-\-no\-check
lists items without checkboxes.
.B \-\-out\-file
writes to a file instead of standard output (an
.B .html
extension selects HTML). The list filters scope the manifest.
.TP
.BI "key " "set|get|rm"
Manage a backend's key in the system keyring; needs
.BR \-\-backend ,
and an optional
.B \-\-user
to keep several accounts of one backend apart (the plain form is the default
account, a named one is used only when the same
.B \-\-user
is given to
.B index
or
.BR sync ).
.B set
reads a key from the terminal without echoing it (or from standard input when
piped) and stores it;
.B get
prints the stored key;
.B rm
removes it. Once a key is stored, commands read it from the keyring
automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Selection and credentials
.TP
.BI "\-\-backend " name
Backend to use (see
.BR BACKENDS ).
.TP
.BI "\-\-user " name
The Bandcamp fan\-page handle, and the keyring account to use (see
.BR key );
the plain form, with no
.BR \-\-user ,
is the default account.
.TP
.BI "\-\-bundle " ref
Restrict
.B index
or
.B sync
to a single bundle named by
.IR ref ,
instead of the whole collection. For itch.io the reference is a bundle link
.RB ( https://itch.io/b/ \fIid\fR / \fIslug\fR ), its numeric id, or a unique part
of its title; run
.B bundles
to list them. Only items you own from that bundle are listed. Bundle download
links
.RB ( https://itch.io/bundle/download/ \fItoken\fR )
are not accepted; they need a browser session. A subset
.B index
does not sweep, so it will not mark the rest of your library removed. A backend
that does not support subsets reports so. A resolved subset is cached under
.I <data dir>/cache
for a day and reused;
.B \-\-refresh
ignores the cache and re\-fetches.
.B \-\-bundle
and
.B \-\-creator
cannot be combined.
.TP
.BI "\-\-creator " name
Restrict
.B index
or
.B sync
to one creator's items, matched by itch username (the subdomain of a page URL),
by display name, or by a page URL. Run
.B creators
to list the creators in your index. Like
.BR \-\-bundle ,
a subset
.B index
does not sweep. The same one\-day cache applies.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Re\-resolve items that are already fully downloaded.
.B sync
skips such items by default, without contacting the store, so a repeat run
finishes quickly; pass this to re\-resolve them and pick up a store\-side
re\-upload. A partially downloaded item is always resolved so it can be
completed. This flag also ignores any cached
.B \-\-bundle
or
.B \-\-creator
result and resolves it again from the network.
.TP
.BI "\-\-app\-key " key
Application or API key (DriveThruRPG, itch.io). Exposes the key in the process
list; prefer the keyring or the file form.
.TP
.BI "\-\-app\-key\-file " path
Read the application or API key from a file, so it never appears on the command
line.
.TP
.BI "\-\-cookies " path
Cookies file (Bandcamp, and itch.io for session\-gated downloads): a Firefox
cookies.sqlite, a Cookie Quick Manager JSON export, or a Netscape cookies.txt.
.TP
.B \-\-firefox
Load cookies from the Firefox profiles on this machine. Bandcamp needs them to
download; itch.io needs them only for items whose entitlement lives in the web
session, such as bundle items, which the API key alone cannot fetch.
.SS Storage and content
.TP
.BI "\-\-db " path
Index database. Defaults to the config
.B db
key, or
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/magicdl.sqlite
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/magicdl/
when that variable is set).
.TP
.BI "\-\-out " dir
Output directory. Required; taken from the config
.B out
key when not given. There is no built\-in default.
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " list
Content formats, comma\-separated. For a single\-file backend (Bandcamp) the
first entry is the audio format to request
.RB ( flac ", " vorbis " for ogg, " mp3\-320 ", ...)."
For multi\-file backends the list keeps only those file types (for example
.BR pdf ", " pdf,epub ).
Unset means
.B flac
for Bandcamp and every file elsewhere.
.TP
.B \-\-covers
Also download cover images (Bandcamp).
.TP
.B \-\-from\-index
For
.BR sync :
download from the stored index without listing from the store.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-hidden
Skip hidden collection items when indexing.
.SS verify
.TP
.B \-\-rehash
Re\-hash present files to check integrity.
.TP
.B \-\-rescan
Relocate moved files by content hash, scanning
.BR \-\-out .
.SS list filters
.TP
.BI "\-\-status " s
Only items with this status
.RB ( active ", " removed ", " preorder ", " unavailable ).
.TP
.B \-\-hidden ", " \-\-blacklisted ", " \-\-superseded
Only items with the named flag.
.TP
.B \-\-downloaded ", " \-\-not\-downloaded
Only items that are, or are not, downloaded.
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " n
Cap the number of items.
.SS manifest
.TP
.BI "\-\-out\-file " path
Write the manifest to this file instead of standard output. An
.B .html
extension selects HTML output.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Write the manifest as HTML rather than Markdown.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-check
Omit the download checkboxes and the download tally.
.SS index
.TP
.B \-\-hashes
Also resolve each item's files from the store and record their hashes in the
index (itch.io), so
.B reorganize \-\-hash
can match offline. Resumable; combine with
.B \-\-refresh
to re\-resolve items whose hashes are already stored.
.SS reorganize
.TP
.B \-\-hash
Also sort the loose files of multi\-owner hosts by matching their hashes against
the store\-side upload hashes (otherwise such hosts are left for a later run).
The hashes come from
.BR "index \-\-hashes" ;
without them the pass resolves from the store on the spot and caches the result.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-cross\-host
Match each remaining loose file against the stored hashes of every owned item on
any host, and move it under that item's real slug folder. Recovers files under a
folder whose name no longer matches the item's host (a renamed itch username).
Implies
.BR \-\-hash ,
is offline, and needs
.BR "index \-\-hashes" .
.TP
.BI "\-\-max\-owned " n
With
.BR \-\-hash ,
skip a host that owns more than
.I n
items, so a large shared host is not resolved. Unset or 0 means no limit.
.SS Output and pacing
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output for
.BR status ", " list ", " details ", " verify ", " blacklist ", " allow ", " relocate ", and " forget .
.TP
.BI "\-\-interval\-ms " n
Base delay between requests. Default 3000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-retries " n
Retries per request. Default 5.
.TP
.BI "\-\-timeout\-ms " n
Per\-request timeout. Default 30000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-user\-agent " s
The HTTP User\-Agent header sent with every request. Defaults to
.RI magicdl/ version ,
or the config
.B user\-agent
key. Set it when a store expects a particular client string.
.TP
.BI "\-\-reason " text
Note why an item is blacklisted.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and report without writing files.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B bandcamp
Audio. Authenticates with browser cookies
.RB ( \-\-firefox " or " \-\-cookies )
and needs
.BR \-\-user .
An album arrives as a zip, which is unpacked in place into
.IR <Artist> / "<year> \- <Title>" .
.TP
.B drivethrurpg
RPG PDFs and files. Authenticates with an application key from the account's
"Library App Keys" page.
.TP
.B itchio
Games, tools, and assets. Authenticates with an API key from
itch.io/user/settings/api\-keys. Session\-gated items, such as bundle items,
also need browser cookies
.RB ( \-\-firefox " or " \-\-cookies )
to download: the API key alone cannot fetch them. Downloads mirror the store
layout,
.IR <user> .itch.io/ <slug> ,
taken from each item's page URL, rather than the default
.IR Creator " - " Title
folder.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Bandcamp uses your logged\-in browser session cookies. DriveThruRPG and itch.io
use an application or API key.
.PP
The preferred store for a key is the system keyring, the freedesktop Secret
Service served by GNOME Keyring or KWallet, reached through
.B libsecret
loaded at run time. Store a key with
.RB "\[dq]" "magicdl key set \-\-backend " name "\[dq]"
and later commands read it automatically. When no keyring is available, keep
the key in a file readable only by you and pass
.B \-\-app\-key\-file
so the secret does not appear in the process list.
.PP
A key is resolved in this order, first match wins:
.BR \-\-app\-key ,
then
.B \-\-app\-key\-file
or the config
.BR app\-key\-file ,
then the keyring, then a bare
.B app\-key
in the config. A configured key file therefore overrides the keyring.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/magicdl/config.ini
Optional config file
.RB ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magicdl/config.ini
when that variable is set). A
.B [general]
section and a
.BI [backend. name ]
section per backend set defaults for
.BR db ", " out ", " user ", " app\-key\-file ", " cookies ", and " format .
A backend section overrides
.BR [general] ,
and a command\-line option overrides both. Paths may use
.B ~
and environment variables.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/magicdl.sqlite
Default index database
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/magicdl/
when set; override with
.B \-\-db
or the config
.B db
key). The index is a rebuildable cache and holds no secrets. If it is corrupted
and will not open, delete it together with any
.BR \-journal ", " \-wal ", or " \-shm
sidecar file next to it
.RB ( "rm magicdl.sqlite*" )
and run
.B index
again to rebuild it; downloaded files are untouched.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/cache/
Cached
.B \-\-bundle
and
.B \-\-creator
resolutions, reused for a day. Safe to delete;
.B \-\-refresh
also rewrites them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Index a DriveThruRPG library:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl index \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey
.EE
.RE
.PP
Download everything not yet fetched, from the index, without re\-listing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey \-\-out ~/rpg \-\-from\-index \-\-not\-downloaded
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fetch only the PDFs of an item:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey \-\-out ~/rpg \-\-format pdf 12345
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sync a Bandcamp collection as ogg:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend bandcamp \-\-user yourhandle \-\-firefox \-\-out ~/music \-\-format vorbis
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sync only one itch.io creator's items:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend itchio \-\-creator willibab \-\-out ~/itch
.EE
.RE
.SH RATE LIMITING
Some stores are quick to rate limit and slow to forgive. Requests are spaced out
and backed off after an HTTP 429. The defaults are conservative;
.B \-\-interval\-ms
sets a faster base pace when an account tolerates it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B magicdl
exits 0 on success, 1 on an error, and 2 on an unknown command.
.SH COPYRIGHT
PUBLIC DOMAIN (CC0\-1.0).
